# Generate Commit Message (sparkles)

Cursor Source Control sparkles only reads this file (not `.cursor/rules` or AGENTS.md).

## Hard output rules

- Output **exactly** two lines of English (subject, blank line is optional, then one body line). Prefer no blank line if the UI allows a single subject+body block as two lines.
- **Total length ≤ ~120 characters** across both lines. Shorter is better.
- No bullets, no file lists, no PR descriptions, no "Made-with: Cursor", no trailing period on the subject.

## Format

```text
<type>: <topic>

<why>
```

1. `<type>`: one of `feat` | `fix` | `docs` | `refactor` | `test` | `chore` | `perf` | `ci`
2. `<topic>`: **2–5 words**, area only. Max ~40 characters after the colon.
   - Do **not** use verbs (`update`, `add`, `implement`, `refactor`, `improve`, `change`, `fix`).
   - Do **not** name files/components as a changelog (`OutbreakMap`, `route.ts`).
3. `<why>`: **one short sentence** (≤ ~15 words) on purpose only — why this exists for the user/system.
   - Do **not** list what changed, how it was done, or multiple edits joined with "and".

## Good

```text
feat: map loading UI

Show basemap as soon as MapLibre loads.
```

```text
refactor: thin basemap style

Shrink style payload so the map paints sooner.
```

## Bad (never generate)

```text
refactor: update OutbreakMap to use thin basemap style

Replace hardcoded basemap URLs with a dynamic style function and adjust zoom levels for improved map performance.
```

```text
Refactor OutbreakMap loading logic and improve error handling

- Enhanced the loading process...
- Improved error handling...
```
